# Secrets - never commit. verbatra loads .env automatically and reads the
# provider key (GEMINI_API_KEY) from the environment only. The root .gitignore
# already ignores these; this local copy makes the boundary explicit and mirrors
# what `verbatra init` scaffolds for any consuming project.
.env
.env.local

# ...but the template (key name only, no real value) is meant to be committed.
!.env.example

# verbatra's local-only run-status snapshot (review flags, token usage); never committed.
.verbatra-local/
verbatra.cache.json

# Generated from packages/cli/package.json by scripts/sync-version.mjs, which dev, build and
# typecheck all run first. Tracking it meant every local docs run dirtied the working tree and the
# committed copy drifted behind the published version (it sat three releases stale), sweeping
# resync noise into unrelated pull requests. Nothing user-facing depended on the committed value:
# the sync runs before `next build`, so the deployed site always showed the correct version.
lib/version.generated.json
